{
  "info": {
    "name": "KairoX \u00b7 Cutting",
    "description": "The grid that replaced the cutting manager's spreadsheet. One row is ONE garment; hides are allocated to it, edited freely while DRAFT, then frozen by an audited approval.\n\nSETUP\n  1. Import the whole folder and SELECT the KairoX environment\n     (top-right). That is what shares one token across every\n     collection \u2014 a collection variable is visible only to the\n     collection that set it.\n  2. Run `user` \u2192 Login. Its test script stores `access_token` for\n     you; there is nothing to copy and paste.\n  3. Every request here inherits bearer auth from that token.\n\n`base_url` defaults to http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nOptional query params are present but DISABLED, so each request runs\nas-is. File uploads are real form-data rows \u2014 click Select Files on\nthe `file` row. Generated from the app's own OpenAPI schema by\n`python scripts/make_postman_per_service.py` \u2014 re-run it after changing\nroutes rather than editing requests by hand.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{token}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Add Sheet",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/cutting/rows/{{row_id}}/sheets",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "cutting",
            "rows",
            "{{row_id}}",
            "sheets"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "row_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "The cutter needed one more skin. TYPE ITS MEASUREMENT, scan it, or pick it.\n\n`dcm` alone is the normal path and it is a LOOKUP: the number written on the\nskin resolves to that hide of this row's article and colour, and the reply\nsays which code it matched. Nothing of that article in stock is a 422 saying\nso plainly \u2014 there is no sheet available to cut this row from.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"sheet_code\": \"\",\n  \"sheet_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"material_lot_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n  \"dcm\": 0,\n  \"dcm_tolerance\": 0,\n  \"create_if_missing\": false\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Approve",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/cutting/rows/{{row_id}}/approve",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "cutting",
            "rows",
            "{{row_id}}",
            "approve"
          ],
          "variable": [
            {
              "key": "row_id",
              "value": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Freeze the row: these hides, this total, THIS cutter.\n\n`cutter_employee_id` is named HERE, one garment at a time \u2014 `generate` takes\nno cutter, because one id there put the same worker on every row of the\nstyle and the cutting row is what a piece rate is paid from.\n\n`user.id` is an app_user id \u2014 the LOGIN \u2014 which is what AuditLog.actor_user_id\nrequires. The WORKER is the row's cutter_employee_id and is a different\nperson in a different table.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"cutter_employee_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Assign Cutters",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/cutting/rows/assign",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "cutting",
            "rows",
            "assign"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Save the grid's cutter column \u2014 a different worker per garment.\n\nThe bulk form of PATCH /cutting/rows/{id}. Partial accept: a frozen row comes\nback in `rejected` and never loses the rows that did assign.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"assignments\": [\n    {\n      \"row_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\",\n      \"cutter_employee_id\": \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "response": []
    },
